# API base for production builds (`npm run build`).
#
# The backend is hosted on Railway, so the built frontend talks to it directly
# across origins. That means the Railway service MUST list this frontend's own
# origin in CORS_ORIGINS, or every request is rejected with 403.
#
# If you instead serve the frontend from the same host as the API (the nginx
# vhost in deploy.md proxies /api to a local backend), delete this file so the
# client falls back to the same-origin default of "/api" and CORS never applies.
VITE_API_URL=https://rentoni-production.up.railway.app/api
